\section{Caching}{
 Compiled functions are cached on disk the same way
compiled models are (see \code{\link[=stan_model]{stan_model()}}) -- a warm cache skips
recompilation entirely, including across R sessions.
}

\section{Serialization}{
 Exposed function objects in \verb{$functions} are
compiled bindings and, like any compiled function from this package, do
not survive \code{saveRDS()}/\code{readRDS()}. After restoring a saved
\code{\link{StanModel}} or \code{\link{StanFit}}, call \verb{$expose_stan_functions()} again to
repopulate \verb{$functions} -- this rebuilds from the on-disk cache and
does not recompile.
}

